    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\nHi,\r\nI think it would be very nice trying to implement some features of [mucomplete](https://github.com/lifepillar/vim-mucomplete), which is a simple wrapper around vim's completion, such as chained completions.",
